🔍 What a DevSecOps Engineer Actually Does in a Day.

Most people think DevSecOps is just “running pipelines.”
The reality is much more systems, security, and problem-solving.

Here’s a snapshot of my typical day as a DevSecOps Engineer.

⚙️ Reviewing merge requests & pipeline results
 🔐 Checking security scans & vulnerability reports
 ☁️ Monitoring cloud resources & environment health
 🐳 Troubleshooting Docker/Kubernetes deployments
 🏗️ Updating Terraform/IaC for infra changes
 📊 Looking at logs, metrics & deployment performance
 🤝 Syncing with dev & QA teams for smooth releases

Biggest lesson:
 👉 DevSecOps isn’t about tools — it’s about making systems reliable for people who build and use them.
